==== stdout ====
Usage: raphael restore <path> [options]
       raphael restore --id <id> [options]

Remove an item’s own archive cause.

Restore removes only the item’s own archive cause. If a parent remains archived,
the item stays archived and the answer names the parent to restore.

An already active item succeeds without a change.

Archive causes print one per line, nearest first: directly, or through the
archived container above the item, then who set the cause in parentheses. (user)
is a cause set with archive; restore removes only that cause, and only on the
item itself. JSON carries each cause as origin, owner and reason.

Options:
      --id <id>
          Address by stable id instead of path.
      --revision <n>
          Revision read previously. When omitted, it is read just before
          sending.
      --json
          Print the result as one JSON document.
  -h, --help
          Show help.

Examples:
  raphael restore /work/raphael
  raphael restore --id 42
  raphael restore --id 42 --revision 8 --json

Prints:
  The item with its path, revision and remaining archive causes. Still archived,
  with the restore command for the container, when a container keeps it
  archived; Unchanged when nothing was removed. JSON carries `node`,
  `archiveCauses` and `changed`.

Next: raphael get --id 42

See also: raphael help archive; raphael help revisions
